    "scope": "Surviving southeast pronaos corner: exactly three fluted pale Corinthian columns with moulded bases, leafy/corner-volute capitals and the broken L-shaped surviving entablature, with low mapped podium/cella wall fragments and an open destroyed temple interior. No intact cella, roof, full pediment, complete peristyle or ancient full-temple reconstruction. Preserve Tabularium and independent neighboring ruins."
